Evaluate signed official KGlobalAccelD 6.7.5 as a scoped private SDK source
transition. Preserve the Ubuntu three-binary profile, SONAME0, development SDK,
XCB backend, autostart/systemd payloads and default deprecated public D-Bus API.
No KDE/Qt source patch, excluded feature, skipped native test or Qt replacement.

The unchanged original public application must pass before and after an actual
APT upgrade: real owned XTEST keys, QAction activation, legacy methods, defaults,
conflict, block/unblock and removal. Qt package identities remain unchanged.
Record and preserve the installed original KWin Wayland/X11 runtime executables
and both libraries, versions and bytes through the package upgrade; APT check
must pass. Full installed KWin sessions and other applications remain later QA.

The installed private headers explicitly designate a private API. Upstream
changed QList<QKeySequence> to QSet under the same SONAME, removed ten reviewed
private/implementation exports and changed both getters' return ABI while
retaining their mangled names. Do not report the old private executable as
compatible: retain its exact bytes and require the observed loader exit127 with
the exact removed foreign QList setter and no functional output. Unrelated
failures, successful execution or another missing symbol are fatal. Separately
recompile the identical private client source and require its full assertions.
The original private baseline remains mandatory before candidate installation.

The symbols proposal preserves189 unaffected guard lines, raises both changed
getters to upstream6.7.5, records21 verified new exports and four explicitly
observed optional amd64 templates. Daemon/runtime/dev versions are locked
exactly. The sealed Attempt1 failure and prior guard review remain unchanged.
All three official native tests and generated AppStream tests remain fatal and
run serially inside disposable clean sbuild; lintian and installed package gates
remain mandatory. Private Xvfb, closed D-Bus, process groups and state are reaped.

Existing zero-NIC KVM evidence covers original daemon/plugin, original KWin
Wayland and KWin X11 with frozen original/candidate library providers and
unchanged public contracts. It is diagnostic evidence, not a candidate .deb
build or installed APT upgrade. This staging proposal remains unadmitted until
its scoped lifecycle and a fresh authoritative input preflight are reviewed.
Undeclared third-party private binaries receive no compatibility assertion.
Final Ubuntu application/desktop/release compatibility gates remain required.

The three KConfigGroup template exports absent from the reviewed original
amd64 library also require the reviewed6.7.5 provider. Their prior minimum
versions described armhf/riscv64 entries and must not silently apply to the
new amd64 entries. The single widened entry now uses the conservative6.7.5
minimum; non-amd64 packages remain outside this certification. The original
architecture-qualified metadata and all prior reviews are retained unchanged.
